<title>NIGERIA: Nigeria's weekly forex demand rises to $90.36 mln.</title>
<headline>Nigeria's weekly forex demand rises to $90.36 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's central bank said on Friday it sold $90.36 million at a rate of 80 to the dollar at its weekly auction.</p>
<p>Last week, the bank sold $76.9 at the same rate.</p>
<p>Bankers said the increased demand indicated business was picking up after the fiscal 1997 budget was released three weeks ago.</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
